<title>CANADA: Ag Canada sets 96/97 and 97/98 grain/oilseed S &amp; D.</title>
<headline>Ag Canada sets 96/97 and 97/98 grain/oilseed S &amp; D.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Canada on Tuesday revised its 1996/97 (Aug/July) supply and disposition of grains and oilseeds and issued its first forecast for 1997/98.</p>
<p>CROP/YEAR HARVESTED YIELD OUTPUT SUPPLY EXPORT CARRYOUT PRICE</p>
<p>	     '000 ha   t/ha  (thousands of metric tonnes) C$/t</p>
<p>DURUM WHEAT</p>
<p>1997/98   2,178     2.222  4,840  6,845  3,900  2,100  185-215</p>
<p>1996/97   2,096     2.243  4,703  6,731  3,850  2,000  203-233</p>
<p>1995/96   2,125     2.188  4,648  6,116  3,222  2,023    286*</p>
<p>WHEAT EXCEPT DURUM</p>
<p>1997/98  10,080     2.343 23,620 29,735 17,000  5,700  165-195</p>
<p>1996/97  10,556     2.443 25,792 30,428 16,900  6,100  194-214</p>
<p>1995/96   9,017     2.259 20,369 24,601 12,977  4,610    254*</p>
<p>ALL WHEAT</p>
<p>1997/98  12,258     2.322 28,460 36,580 20,900  7,800</p>
<p>1996/97  12,652     2.410 30,495 37,158 20,750  8,100</p>
<p>1995/96  11,141     2.245 25,017 30,717 16,198  6,633</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
